From c55671b1af9d6d4275b337b83709cb17fcfe2655 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:28:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] fix(agent): stop runaway turns, honor /stop, and bound
 tool batches
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

K2 intermittently returns tool calls as text in `content` instead of native
tool_calls. On a cut or max_tokens-truncated stream the XML fallback parsed
that partial text into 73/366 tool calls and executed them, and the user
could not stop the turn: "/stop" was dropped by the queue_mode=off busy gate
and the provider stream was uninterruptible.

- Route stop-like commands centrally in SessionManager.routeInbound: when a
  turn is running, requestTurnInterrupt instead of dropping, so /stop works
  on every channel path (daemon/Slack, channel_loop, callbacks, sync Telegram).
- Handle stop-like commands at enqueue time in the daemon inbound dispatcher:
  each session maps to one sharded FIFO worker, so a Slack /stop for a busy
  session used to sit behind the very turn it had to interrupt and routeInbound
  was never reached. Signal the interrupt before sharding and drop the message;
  FIFO is preserved for everything else (mirrors the Telegram worker fast-path).
- Make gateway logging non-blocking: a custom std_options.logFn formats into a
  bounded ring drained by one thread, so a wedged stderr write (full docker
  json-file log pipe) can no longer park a turn on the process-global stderr
  lock. Producers never block; they drop and count. Verified: a blocked pipe
  write leaves 1 thread in anon_pipe_write and the rest in futex_do_wait.
- Return a distinct error.Interrupted from curlStream when the cancel watcher
  fired (even before any bytes arrived) or when a /stop killed curl mid-upload
  (the stdin write then fails), and propagate it through the compatible
  streaming fallback and the retry loops without retrying — including the
  post-vision-error retry stream, which must not surface a raw error or degrade
  the route for a user-initiated stop. The agent ends the turn with the normal
  interrupt reply.
- Stop the cancel watcher before killing/reaping curl (PID-reuse window),
  following the established http_util.abortCurlChild ordering.
- Propagate a `truncated` flag from the providers to the agent and refuse to
  execute tool calls parsed from a truncated response. Set it on cut recovery
  paths, on `finish_reason=="length"`, and on the non-streaming parsers that
  were previously unflagged: Anthropic `stop_reason=="max_tokens"`, Gemini/
  Vertex `finishReason=="MAX_TOKENS"`, and the Responses API `status=="incomplete"`
  (or `incomplete_details.reason=="max_output_tokens"`).
- Detect finish_reason=="length" with a textual scan instead of a size-limited
  JSON parse, so a >16 KB data line no longer hides a max_tokens cut.
- Cap tool calls per batch (24) and reject an oversized batch wholesale.
- Make the provider stream interruptible: thread the agent interrupt flag
  into curlStream and kill the curl child when it is raised.
- Keep the per-call tool logs off the hot path (debug) so a large batch
  cannot hammer the process-global log lock inside the session turn.

Regression tests cover each change.
